    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Parts a and b are signposted: differentiate, then compute the discriminant of the derivative. The essential demand is in part c. The student must reframe 'never decreasing' as f'(x)≥0 for all x. They must then link this to an upward-opening quadratic that never goes below the x-axis, and so to discriminant ≤0, including the inclusive boundary k=12. This is a linked routine procedure with one conceptual reframing. The discriminant is supplied, and there is no asymptote or domain subtlety. That makes it slightly harder than p13-practice and clearly easier than p17-q14.",
